In article <1815@castle.ed.ac.uk> egnr69@castle.ed.ac.uk (I Chisholm) writes:
>When blessing/cursing items on altars, do you bless items by dropping
>them on an altar of your own allegiency (and curse by dropping onto the
>opposite allegiency) or is it bless/lawful altar and curse/chaotic altar
>no matter who you follow. Wouldn't the first idea be more logical?
>

  The only thing you can bless/curse by dropping on an altar is water:  it
becomes holy water when dropped on a lawful altar, unholy water when dropped
on a chaotic altar, and just plain uncursed water when dropped on a neutral
altar.  Other things can then be blessed/cursed by being dipped in the
water.

  This of course makes it very advantageous to be a lawful character, since 
they can by sacrificing convert any altar to lawfulness and then be able to
create holy water.

	-- Bill Skaggs


